<title>UK: Clarke plans rigorous corporate tax monitoring.</title>
<headline>Clarke plans rigorous corporate tax monitoring.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said he planned more rigorous monitoring of corporate taxes.</p>
<p>&quot;Inland Revenue tax experts will be redeployed to investigate even more rigorously how some big, sophisticated companies seem to pay so little tax,&quot; he said in a speech to parliament on his annual 1997/8 budget.</p>
<p>&quot;They will make sure that companies are paying what they owe. In short, we intend to do more about companies being &quot;economical with their tax&quot;,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
</text>
